{# A member's own context in a shared workspace (`middleware/member_context`).
   Sent only on calls in that member's streak, appended to its first message,
   and never stored. Byte-identical for equal inputs: it sits inside the
   cached prefix for the rest of the streak. Every value is read per turn and
   escaped by the caller; `name` is the member's tag name, `preferences`
   their answer preferences (answer_preferences, without proactivity),
   `memory` their index or None. `folder` is where the file tools read their
   memory, None for a build without that route. #}
{% if name %}
<member_context>
{{ name }} wrote every member message from here on, and this is {{ name }}'s own context, which the harness gives you only on their messages. The other members read everything you write in this thread: use it only as far as {{ name }}'s request needs, and keep it out of workspace memory, agent.md, notes and every other file.
{% if not preferences.empty %}

## How {{ name }} wants answers
{% set member = name %}
{% include "components/agent_preferences.md.j2" %}
{% endif %}
{% if memory is not none %}

## {{ name }}'s memory
{% if folder %}

Read-only here. Read the files the index points to with Read at `{{ folder }}`; Bash, ExecuteCode and Grep cannot reach that folder, and a change to it is {{ name }}'s to make from their own workspace.
{% endif %}

<memory{% if folder %} path="{{ folder }}memory.md"{% endif %}>
{{ memory }}
</memory>
{% endif %}
</member_context>
{% endif %}
